Strategy Note - ES Futures</div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:12px;\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #34d399;border-radius:10px;padding:14px;\"><div style=\"color:#34d399;text-transform:uppercase;\">Base Case</div><p style=\"color:#e2e8f0;font-size:13px;\">ES 7839.50 overnight holds above the Sep 22 SPY 773.38 close context. With MOVE 78.56 calm and the 10Y 4.96%, favor measured continuation only while the opening structure and Treasury supply absorption hold. Keep size defined around Barr at 10:05 AM and EIA at 10:30 AM.</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #f87171;border-radius:10px;padding:14px;\"><div style=\"color:#f87171;text-transform:uppercase;\">Invalidation</div><p style=\"color:#e2e8f0;font-size:13px;\">A decisive ES break of the overnight range alongside a sharp 10Y rebound or MOVE crossing 80 invalidates the calm continuation thesis. Reassess after the 1:00 PM funding release; do not chase the first data reaction.</p></div></div></div>"}